<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>Label</key>
    <string>com.convivy.issue-pr-reconcile</string>

    <!-- Closes a `pr-open` issue once its fix PR merges.

         `issue_link_pr` moves an issue to `pr-open` and calls the state
         non-terminal: the issue stays open "until the PR merges, when you
         issue_resolve it fixed." Nothing performed that second half, so an issue
         whose fix shipped stayed pr-open forever and kept counting as active work.

         Measured 2026-07-30: of 59 active issues, 39 were pr-open and 14 of those
         had already-merged PRs. The queue read as a growing backlog while the crew
         was draining it, and the morning number drifted further from the truth
         every night.

         05:30, between the 03:30 fleet drain and the 06:00 morning report. That
         ordering is the point rather than a convenience: the drain opens the PRs
         that move issues INTO pr-open, and the report reads the queue to tell the operator
         what is waiting on him. Reconciling between the two means the number he
         reads at 06:00 counts only PRs that are genuinely still open.

         Safe to overlap with anything: it only ever transitions pr-open → fixed
         for a PR GitHub reports MERGED, and the transition is idempotent (a second
         pass finds the issue no longer pr-open and never sees it). A PR closed
         without merging is reported, never resolved — that fix was abandoned, so
         the issue is live work again and the call is a human's.

         PATH carries /opt/homebrew/bin for `gh`; the tool also resolves it
         absolutely (ARCH-086), so the PATH here is belt-and-braces. -->

    <!-- Deploy-pinned per platform/decisions/0059 rule 1
         (issue_01M19RRWSS9ETR09N9M2BJPA0Q): a timer firing unattended is
         production USE of issue-pr-reconcile, not someone working on it, so this reads
         a COPY installed from `main` into ~/.local/deploy/agent-platform-shared/
         (rules 2, 6, 7) instead of the ~/.local/bin symlink into the checkout —
         that symlink still exists and still reaches the tree, for the person who
         re-invokes issue-pr-reconcile interactively while working on it (rule 5).
         bin/agent-platform-autopull refreshes the deploy area on every
         origin/main advance; bin/install-agent-platform-shared is what actually
         builds it.
         ProgramArguments names the deploy area's own pinned interpreter
         explicitly (rule 4), not the shebang or launchd's PATH. -->
    <key>ProgramArguments</key>
    <array>
        <string>__HOME__/.local/deploy/agent-platform-shared/venv/bin/python3</string>
        <string>__HOME__/.local/deploy/agent-platform-shared/bin/issue-pr-reconcile</string>
    </array>

    <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
    <string>__HOME__/.local/deploy/agent-platform-shared</string>

    <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
    <dict>
        <key>PATH</key>
        <string>__HOME__/.local/bin:/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin</string>
    </dict>

    <key>StartCalendarInterval</key>
    <dict>
        <key>Hour</key>
        <integer>5</integer>
        <key>Minute</key>
        <integer>30</integer>
    </dict>

    <key>RunAtLoad</key>
    <false/>

    <key>StandardOutPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/Convivy/agent-runs/issue-pr-reconcile.out.log</string>

    <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
    <string>__HOME__/Convivy/agent-runs/issue-pr-reconcile.err.log</string>
</dict>
</plist>
